            <creation xml:id="creation_3e3d59ce">
               <date enddate="1853-08-13" startdate="1853-07-28" xml:id="date_92c9ffb3">28 July 1853 to 13 Aug. 1853</date>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_174b39e0">
               <p xml:id="idm95">This was the first time Hartmann had one of his works published by Breitkopf &amp; Härtel in Leipzig. Therefore, he asked his son-in-law, Niels W. Gade, to negotiate with the publishers. The songs were dedicated to Gade's wife, Sophie. Opus 55 was also used for "Novellette i sex Smaastykker", probably because Breitkopf &amp; Härtel did not coordinate with C.C. Lose &amp; Delbanco in Copenhagen. No. 1 is dated 28 July 1853; No. 2 6 Aug. 1853; No. 3 undated, probably because it is the same date as Nos. 4-5; No. 5 dated 11 Aug. 1853, and No. 6 13 Aug. 1853.</p>
            </history>
